WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.400
-Naomi, welcome back.
It is always great to see you.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.701
I missed you.
-It's been a minute.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.267
-It's been a minute, yeah.
-A long minute.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.267
-How does it feel to be in
front of an audience?

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:09.701
-I mean, it's been
a while, and --

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:13.200
-Yes. It's the best!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.334
I'm so happy you came in person.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.133
We really appreciate this
and coming to the show.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:22.467
I recently saw a photo of
you and our pal Billy Crudup,

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.534
who we love, on the red carpet
of the SAG Awards.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:28.167
There you guys are there.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.667
And is this the first --
is this the first, like,

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:35.434
red carpet I think I've seen in
like 2 1/2 years or something.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:39.968
-Definitely. It was nice to be
back and, you know,

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.601
get frocked up and everything.

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.767
-Yeah. Is that what they call --
-Frocked up?

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:46.167
Do you say that?
-I mean, the night is young.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.467
Yeah, we can always --
We can get --

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.334
If you want to get --
We got time.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:50.501
You want to get
frocked up tonight?

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:52.467
We can do it.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:55.934
We've got champagne.
You guys want to get frocked up?

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Let's do it.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:01:00.868
♪♪

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.167
I guess that means "dressed up."

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.200
Is that what you're saying?
Yeah?

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.200
-Yes.
-Okay, yeah, of course.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.100
-Put the frocks on.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.234
-"Put the frocks" --
Okay, gotcha.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.300
-Okay. And, yeah, it was nice.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.534
It was a good night to be back
and see old friends

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.767
that you haven't seen for
a while and --

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.100
-It is, right?
-Yeah.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.567
-You get to see everybody and
you go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.100
You don't realize how much --
How many people you miss

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.267
until you're in a room.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:21.100
-It just, like, disappeared,
all that time,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.400
and then there you are.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.667
-Well, you've been to
so many award shows.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.267
One of your movies,
"The Impossible," the --

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.868
I think it was 10 -- You got an
Oscar nomination for that.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.434
That's ten years ago?
-Yeah.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.734
-Is that possible?
-Yeah.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.067
-And I wanted to show
this picture,

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.534
'cause your son in the movie
was a man by the name of

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:37.567
Tom Holland.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.033
-That's right.
-And --

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, you've heard of him.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.667
[ Laughs ]

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.100
-Wait. What was --
Did you have any idea

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.367
that he was going to be one of
the biggest stars

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.801
on the planet?

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:51.634
-I mean, I knew he had a future.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:54.701
-I could tell that he was
a brilliant actor.

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.901
He came with great
discipline and focus,

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.334
'cause he was an athlete.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:02.300
And, you know, he was very
dedicated to doing that.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.400
So, I knew he would be --
he would be good.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.701
-Yeah.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:09.267
-And then he also has a really
great, beautiful family,

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:12.701
who keep him grounded,
and -- and a raw talent, so --

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:13.734
-That's pretty cool.

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:15.701
-But I didn't really think,
"Oh, wow,

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.767
this guy's going to be in
'Spider-Man.'"

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:18.801
-Oh, that would've been --
Yeah, that would've been --

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.334
-That would have been
a far-fetched --

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.601
-That would have
been weird, like,

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.133
"This boy will be
Spider-Man one day."

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.000
Like, "Alright."
-Yes. I have a vision.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.267
-"Get back to your
dressing room, take a nap, yeah.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.567
You're a little
frocked up right now."

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.801
But he turned out great.
I love it.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.000
And, obviously,
I love that movie.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.767
You were telling me backstage,
and I did not --

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.601
I could not
guess this about you,

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:40.000
but you were --
You've turned into a car person.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.267
-Well, inadvertently, yeah.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:46.033
I never -- I mean, I love cars,
but I don't obsess over

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.701
how you choose them,
and, you know, I don't have,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:52.734
like, a special brand that I --
you know, I'm attached to.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.434
-No. But then you just recently
got a vehicle and you --

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:59.968
-My favorite car right --
Well, as of now.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.467
But, yeah, it's a mom van.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:06.434
I call it my Hot Wheels.
-Yeah. You got a minivan.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.734
-I've got a minivan.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:10.167
And you can do all kinds of
things with a minivan.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:12.167
Did you know?
You can get frocked up in it!

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.334
-You can?

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.400
You can get frocked up
coming out of a minivan?

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.167
Tell me about the minivan,
'cause I am obsessed.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.934
-Well, seven seats.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.901
You can move furniture,
which I had to do

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.667
in the middle of the pandemic
by myself.

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.567
You can put the surfboards
in there.

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.501
It's great for the beach.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:30.300
You can -- you can do
all kinds of things.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.434
You can have all your friends,
and it just --

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:33.434
And you don't care.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:34.501
-It's like a party van.

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:35.901
-And you don't, like --
-You don't care.

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:37.100
-My kids were embarrassed.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.133
They were like,
"Mom, that is so not cool."

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.567
-Yeah. Your kids are teenagers.
-Yes, they are.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:42.801
-Wow. What happened? When?

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.267
I didn't even know
they were teenagers.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.434
-Yeah, time flew by.
-What's it like?

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:47.634
What are they like?

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.767
-They're great, and, you know,

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:52.167
but they're also
full of teenage angst,

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:55.901
and, you know, they're a little
grumpy at times.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.234
-Yeah.
I have that to look forward to.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:00.267
-Yeah, you're in
the sweet stage still.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.200
-Yeah. You have a great family.
But, please, give them my best.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.000
Like they care about me, but...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.400
They're like, "I don't even know
who that guy is."

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.534
-No, no. They know you.

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:10.267
-Okay, good, good, good.
-They know you.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:11.701
-I want to talk about
your movie.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.534
This is called "Infinite Storm."

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.334
And this is based on
a true story.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:18.167
And it's a wild story.
Can you set up what it's about?

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:22.968
-Yeah, it's about a woman
who's a search-and-rescue woman.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:28.033
And she does the most incredible
rescue this particular time --

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:32.167
a man who's actually gone up to
the mountain to commit suicide.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.701
-Yeah.
-And she risks her life.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.267
She finds him in
literally short --

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:39.834
like as if he's dressed for the
beach, virtually.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.567
And puts her own life at risk.

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:44.100
But what I love about
this film is,

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.267
it's not just a, you know,
high-drama film.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.801
It's also --
There's a lot of poetry in it,

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:54.033
because nature is a
wonderful resource for healing.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.067
She has her demons
that she's battling.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:05:01.801
And -- Yeah, we always,
like, battle our demons

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.968
and we find other ways
for answers.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:07.701
But, literally, the perfect
reminder in this film is that

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.868
nature is there
and it's beautiful

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.634
and it can quiet the mind.

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:15.000
You don't have to have
extreme settings like mountains,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.000
but you can, you know,
just go to the river

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.901
or go to the beach or go to --

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:19.934
-The park or anything
and just get --

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.100
-And just quiet the mind.
-Yeah.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.901
Did you know this story
before the script?

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:25.067
-I did not. I didn't.
-Yeah.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:27.100
-But --
-It's wild.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:30.100
She's doing her normal thing
and she sees these footprints

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.667
that go off the trail and she's
like -- in the snow --

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:34.501
and she's like,
"That's not normal."

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:35.801
-Yes, yeah.
-And then she --

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:36.934
-And they're sneakers.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:39.033
They're not, like,
mountain boots, yeah.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:41.801
And in this extreme weather
this particular day,

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:45.868
nobody should be out there
anyway, much less in sneakers.

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:48.000
-And she cares so much about
saving this --

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.901
It's a pretty fascinating story.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.000
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.767
Here's Naomi Watts in
"Infinite Storm."

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.000
Take a look.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.267
-You belong to this...Pemige--

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:59.934
-Pemigewasset Search and Rescue.

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:03.367
Yeah, that's me, Pam Bales.

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:07.834
-You guys have a helicopter?
-What? A heli--

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.667
[ Laughs ] No, sir.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.400
Just me.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.000
No cellphone service till we get
to the parking lot either.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.601
-No backup, either.

00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:20.300
-Nope. It's just you and me.

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.501
-Come on.

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:33.133
Naomi, I saw that, recently,
you took up pottery.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.467
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:36.734
So -- And I was wondering if
you could maybe show me

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:38.234
how to make something
when we come back.

00:06:38.234 --> 00:06:39.567
-Oh, yeah. Okay.
-Yeah, is that possible? Okay.

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:41.167
More with Naomi Watts
after the break.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.634
Come on back.
We're making pottery!

